--
N5008 [fs.path.construct]/5: path(const Source &) with a std::string source
stores the string, so the path is not empty.  With libstdc++ 13 the
verdict is wrong: path's converting constructor (fs_path.h:330) and
path::_S_convert (fs_path.h:618) are dropped.  _S_convert is a static
member template with a deduced return type whose noexcept-specifier and
`if constexpr' use `is_same_v<typename _Tp::value_type, value_type>';
under libstdc++ the call fails with "found no match for symbol
'is_same_v'" after the constructor's `_S_convert(__detail::__effective_
range(__source))' deduces `<<type:auto>>' for its argument.  A header-free
imitation of _S_convert passes, so the chain through __effective_range /
basic_string_view is needed.  The cvise reduction
(/tmp/r163/red/kb_I, 90 lines) keeps the fs_path.h:330 drop and the
"found no match for symbol 'basic_string'" lookup failure from inside
basic_string's string_view constructor template (_If_sv over a class
derived from decltype(integral_constant<true>)), but degenerated to a
program whose dropped body has no valid specialization ([temp.res.general]/6),
so it is not used as the test; a header-free rewrite of its shape
(/tmp/r163/kb/I7.cpp) shows the lookup failure but neither the drop nor the
wrong verdict.
